> 
> Language definition is basically a small number of large,
> complicated pieces of work, whereas dictionary editing is a large
> number of small, simple units of work. Sit-down sessions as a way
> of doing dictionary work seems particularly ill-suited to me.

I was specifically thinking about things like (1) taking the basic
English list and make sure we have words for everything and (2)
polishing the actual PDF draft until we're happy with printing the
result.

Both seem like things sit-down sessions would work for.  Other than
that, I agree.

